earning","deep-neural-networks","distributed","machine-learning","ml","neural-network","python","tensorflow"],"visibility":"public","forks":75218,"open_issues":3802,"watchers":194125,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tensorflow/tensorflow/pulls/24058","html_url":"https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/pull/24058","diff_url":"https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/pull/24058.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/pull/24058.patch","merged_at":"2018-12-13T21:57:51Z"},"body":"Instead of blocking on completion of an RDMA op, RecvTensor client will now post a work request to the NIC send queue and return immediately. \r\n\r\nThe GDR background polling thread will handle the callback after the corresponding RDMA op is completed, i.e. polled from the completion queue on NIC. The old epoll based mechanism is removed to trade higher CPU usage for improved throughput and lower latencies for RDMA ops.\r\n\r\nThe maximum numbers of work request (WR) in the send/recv queues on NIC are increased to entertain the increased number of concurrent RDMA ops. The threshold of tensor size below which we pass the tensor content in metadata is also increased to reduce the pressure to send/recv queues on NIC.\r\n\r\nThis fixes #23933.\r\n\r\nSigned-off-by: Bairen Yi <byronyi@clustar.ai>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tensorflow/tensorflow/issues/24058/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tensorflow/tensorflow/issues/24058/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":1999635366,"node_id":"MDEzOkFzc2lnbmVkRXZlbnQxOTk5NjM1MzY2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tensorflow/tensorflow/issues/events/1999635366","actor":{"login":"ymodak","id":42785357,"node_i